# Queen's Bay Paladin: "Whenever this creature enters or attacks ..., return up to one target Vampire card from your graveyard". Turn 1
# Bot1 casts Vampire Hexmage and Vampire Interloper (each mana value 2) off two Black Lotuses; both are Bolted on turn 2. On turn 3 the
# Paladin enters and Bot1 chooses no target ("up to one": both Vampires stay in the graveyard and no life is lost, CR 601.2c). On turn 5
# the Paladin attacks: the trigger refuses a Black Lotus (no Vampire) and a second target (only one), returns the Interloper with a
# finality counter, and Bot1 loses 2 life, leaving the Hexmage in the graveyard; Bot2 takes 5 combat damage from the unblocked Paladin.

